{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>That your days may be long.</b> These five commandments, when kept, will lengthen your days — they will bring about for you a length of days without end, in which no diminution occurs, as the Sages said, of blessed memory (Kiddushin 39b): לְעוֹלָם שֶׁכֻּלּוֹ אָרֹךְ (\"a world that is entirely long\"). For indeed the substance of these five commandments is all of it to give honor to El, blessed be He, through which the one who honors Him inherits eternal life. This is: to know Him as the One who brings into being from nothing, to be that Elohim alone is yours, not to serve anything besides Him, not to rebel against Him in thought, in speech, or in deed, and to honor Him — is He not our Father, who acquired us?" "<b>Upon the land.</b> Through keeping them you will merit this: that length of days of which I spoke, you will acquire it while dwelling upon the land, so that you will not be exiled from it. The other five commandments, however — not to harm a person in body, in honor, or in property, in deed, in speech, or in thought — are warnings that protect from punishment in this world and in the world to come."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:32.814743616Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}